# Enforce LF line endings on checkout for all text files, regardless of the
# developer's (or CI runner's) core.autocrlf setting.
#
# Git for Windows (used by the windows-* GitHub Actions runners) ships with
# core.autocrlf=true by default, which converts LF -> CRLF on checkout.
# golangci-lint's gofmt then fails with "File is not properly formatted" on
# every .go file — only the first 3 are surfaced due to max-same-issues: 3.
# Pinning eol=lf here keeps checkouts byte-identical across OSes and resolves
# the Windows-only lint failure. Existing Windows clones should run
# `git add --renormalize .` once after pulling this file.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Go source must always use LF.
*.go text eol=lf
